00:37:30.540 --> 00:37:31.580
I mean, we've seen this too

00:37:31.580 --> 00:37:33.300
with code that's been produced.

00:37:33.300 --> 00:37:36.740
It's not air-free, it needs QA.

00:37:36.740 --> 00:37:40.100
It needs a human to look at,

00:37:40.100 --> 00:37:41.700
we still do need that oftentimes,

00:37:41.700 --> 00:37:44.060
a human to take that step back and look,

00:37:44.060 --> 00:37:45.900
okay, well, it looks right on the surface,

00:37:45.900 --> 00:37:48.380
but does this apply to the right situation?

00:37:48.380 --> 00:37:51.780
Does this make sense for what we're trying to do?

00:37:51.780 --> 00:37:53.580
I think of it like,

00:37:53.580 --> 00:37:56.820
I do lots of UAT testing

00:37:56.820 --> 00:37:58.260
and I think of it like,

00:37:58.260 --> 00:38:00.140
you're passing a bunch of tests,

00:38:00.140 --> 00:38:02.420
you can pass a bunch of tests and get green,

00:38:02.420 --> 00:38:04.260
but are you testing the right thing?

00:38:04.260 --> 00:38:06.100
Does it make sense for your end goal?

00:38:06.100 --> 00:38:07.540
Customers don't care that you did that,

00:38:07.540 --> 00:38:08.700
they just want their problem solved.

00:38:08.700 --> 00:38:09.540
Yes, yeah.

00:38:10.780 --> 00:38:12.900
I get to do that in the background,

00:38:12.900 --> 00:38:16.060
or have people do that with me.

00:38:16.060 --> 00:38:19.760
So we're in a transition phase.

00:38:19.760 --> 00:38:23.480
I mean, I do have optimism

00:38:23.480 --> 00:38:25.040
that we're gonna get through this.

00:38:25.040 --> 00:38:27.360
