I can't, I don't go there every day anymore.

00:38:46.860 --> 00:38:48.540
If I step up my job search, I'll have to,

00:38:48.540 --> 00:38:50.940
but it's difficult.

00:38:52.340 --> 00:38:55.580
So for just a couple of questions left here.

00:38:55.580 --> 00:38:58.340
So you and I, similar experience.

00:38:58.380 --> 00:39:03.380
We were told in different ways that we would need,

00:39:03.380 --> 00:39:04.900
we need more empathy.

00:39:04.900 --> 00:39:08.660
And we took the path of getting a book and ignoring it

00:39:08.660 --> 00:39:10.900
and then eventually figured it out.

00:39:12.410 --> 00:39:13.850
And we've also talked about the fact

00:39:13.850 --> 00:39:15.090
that there's some self-awareness

00:39:15.090 --> 00:39:18.290
that engineering leaders may not know

00:39:18.290 --> 00:39:19.210
they need more empathy.

00:39:19.210 --> 00:39:22.010
Like I worked with a leader once who,

00:39:22.010 --> 00:39:24.450
this was the person who said he had no empathy.

00:39:24.450 --> 00:39:26.010
He had no self-awareness.

00:39:26.010 --> 00:39:27.930
And he was the kind of person who would,

00:39:28.490 --> 00:39:29.650
in an all-hands meeting would say,

00:39:29.650 --> 00:39:31.610
our team has psychological safety.

00:39:31.610 --> 00:39:32.610
And if you don't agree with me,

00:39:32.610 --> 00:39:37.470
we can have a meeting and talk about it.

00:39:37.470 --> 00:39:38.310
Yeah.

00:39:39.870 --> 00:39:44.950
So two questions here.

00:39:44.950 --> 00:39:45.990
I'll ask them one at a time

00:39:45.990 --> 00:39:48.910
versus my normal eight questions in one.

00:39:48.910 --> 00:39:50.110
How should leaders,

00:39:50.110 --> 00:39:53.630
whether they think they need more empathy or not,

00:39:54.510 --> 00:39:56.190
what's the shift in framing?

00:39:56.190 --> 00:39:57.710
Or what should leaders do?

00:39:57.710 --> 00:39:59.670
I'll say, what could they do?

00:39:59.710 --> 00:40:00.710
Any leader do today,

00:40:00.710 --> 00:40:02.310
regardless of their empathy level,

00:40:02.310 --> 00:40:04.710
to improve their empathy?

00:40:04.710 --> 00:40:06.530
How would they start?

00:40:06.530 --> 00:40:08.420
Yeah.

00:40:08.420 --> 00:40:11.780
I mean, it really depends and for the audience

00:40:11.780 --> 00:40:14.580
and depending on your particular situation

00:40:14.580 --> 00:40:15.420
or where you're at.

00:40:15.420 --> 00:40:18.980
But I think the first thing to do for yourself,

00:40:18.980 --> 00:40:21.700
I mean, much like Alan did with his hike

00:40:21.700 --> 00:40:24.100
and the buzz and having that space.

00:40:24.100 --> 00:40:27.180
I'm not saying you have to go on a big hike

00:40:27.180 --> 00:40:28.940
across the West Coast, but taking that.

00:40:28.940 --> 00:40:30.140
Everybody should walk 3,000 miles.

00:40:30.140 --> 00:40:32.660
Everybody should do it, yes.

00:40:32.660 --> 00:40:34.460
But taking that moment of pause,

00:40:34.460 --> 00:40:37.780
and I do find being outdoors for me personally

00:40:37.780 --> 00:40:40.340
is helpful to be outside.

00:40:40.340 --> 00:40:42.580
Even if it's just outside my home,

00:40:42.580 --> 00:40:45.100
if you're in the Northern hemisphere, it is summer.

00:40:45.100 --> 00:40:48.860
So we can get outside a little bit easier in most parts,

00:40:48.860 --> 00:40:51.460
especially North America, if you're listening in.

00:40:52.740 --> 00:40:56.740
I find having that pause away from my screen,

00:40:56.740 --> 00:40:59.780
whether it be my phone, doom scrolling,

00:40:59.780 --> 00:41:03.100
which I am still guilty of doing at times.

00:41:03.100 --> 00:41:06.780
But having that moment set aside for self-awareness,

00:41:06.780 --> 00:41:08.340
even if it's five to 10 minutes

00:41:08.340 --> 00:41:10.660
and thinking about your interactions,

00:41:10.660 --> 00:41:14.340
trying to reflect on how somebody reacted to you,

00:41:14.340 --> 00:41:18.540
try looking at some, just thinking through it

00:41:18.540 --> 00:41:21.060
because we get so busy.

00:41:21.060 --> 00:41:26.060
We are so, I mean, I think a lot of us overstimulated

00:41:26.060 --> 00:41:29.180
in our society today with everything coming at us.

00:41:29.940 --> 00:41:32.340
Taking that pause, be in your head a little bit,

00:41:32.340 --> 00:41:35.060
have that self-awareness and reflect.

00:41:35.060 --> 00:41:36.540
That's the first step.

00:41:36.540 --> 00:41:39.100
And then of course, I mean, getting feedback,

00:41:39.100 --> 00:41:43.980
talking to people that will give you an honest answer,

00:41:43.980 --> 00:41:46.700
even if you don't like the answer.

00:41:46.700 --> 00:41:48.140
It's good to hear that.

00:41:49.190 --> 00:41:50.870
And listen to the answer.

00:41:50.870 --> 00:41:51.750
And listen to the answer.

00:41:51.750 --> 00:41:53.070
It's different for everyone.

00:41:53.070 --> 00:41:56.510
I discovered, even in some of my warmup hikes,

00:41:56.510 --> 00:41:58.950
reason I really wanted to do the PCT

00:41:58.950 --> 00:42:01.510
is I found it, I knew about it my whole life.

00:42:01.510 --> 00:42:03.110
I wanted to do it, but it kind of faded away

00:42:03.110 --> 00:42:03.950
for a long time.

00:42:03.950 --> 00:42:04.790
Then during the pandemic,

00:42:04.790 --> 00:42:07.790
I fell into a YouTube rabbit hole as one does.

00:42:07.790 --> 00:42:09.510
And I reminded about that, I'm gonna do this someday.

00:42:09.510 --> 00:42:11.150
And the timing was right for me to leave my job

00:42:11.150 --> 00:42:12.830
and go do the hike.

00:42:12.830 --> 00:42:15.150
But one of the things I found

00:42:15.150 --> 00:42:19.900
that was just exponentially accelerated through my hike

00:42:19.900 --> 00:42:22.940
was all that time just to think with no screens,

00:42:22.940 --> 00:42:24.860
and not thinking, not like I'm gonna think about this,

00:42:24.860 --> 00:42:27.250
just let my mind wander.

00:42:27.250 --> 00:42:29.650
And I discovered, and it was just great.

00:42:30.650 --> 00:42:31.570
Undescribable.

00:42:33.200 --> 00:42:34.560
And I can replicate that.

00:42:34.560 --> 00:42:39.040
If I get really, if I'm feeling the buzz, I'll say,

00:42:39.040 --> 00:42:40.560
the best thing I can do for myself

00:42:40.560 --> 00:42:45.560
is at the minimum, go for a long walk around Seattle.

00:42:45.600 --> 00:42:50.480
Best, get myself to a trail away from people.

00:42:50.480 --> 00:42:52.320
I like to pick trails that aren't gonna be full of

00:42:52.320 --> 00:42:54.280
people and just walk.

00:42:54.280 --> 00:42:56.680
And do a long, even camping overnight

00:42:56.680 --> 00:42:58.880
because there's no cell reception out there.

00:42:58.920 --> 00:43:03.800
It is so, it's my place.

00:43:03.800 --> 00:43:05.680
And I think everyone needs to find that place.

00:43:05.680 --> 00:43:07.960
And it could be as simple as 10 minutes

00:43:07.960 --> 00:43:11.190
in a darkened room with nothing on

00:43:11.190 --> 00:43:12.910
where you can literally hear the buzz.

00:43:12.910 --> 00:43:14.650
We can hear the background.

00:43:15.860 --> 00:43:17.780
But it could be different for everyone.

00:43:17.780 --> 00:43:20.140
It could be running,

00:43:20.140 --> 00:43:22.100
it could be some sort of other sort of exercise.

00:43:22.100 --> 00:43:23.820
It could be anything.

00:43:23.820 --> 00:43:26.900
I think not enough people take the time to do that.

00:43:26.940 --> 00:43:29.100
They get so caught up in go, go, go.

00:43:29.100 --> 00:43:31.740
And then, and again, I'm guilty of this too.

00:43:31.740 --> 00:43:34.780
So I'm not saying it's hypocritical,

00:43:34.780 --> 00:43:38.420
but we get a moment where we're waiting in line

00:43:38.420 --> 00:43:42.460
or we're just, oh, I got 10 minutes to kill

00:43:42.460 --> 00:43:43.300
before I have to go.

00:43:43.300 --> 00:43:44.120
What do we do?

00:43:44.120 --> 00:43:45.580
We get on our phones and scroll.

00:43:45.580 --> 00:43:49.020
Oh, maybe I missed some world news on Instagram.

00:43:49.020 --> 00:43:49.860
No, you didn't.

00:43:49.860 --> 00:43:54.860
Just, I think finding a way to be present with yourself

00:43:57.140 --> 00:43:58.580
is a great way to grow.

00:43:58.580 --> 00:44:00.940
And then of course, I read a lot.

00:44:00.940 --> 00:44:02.540
